{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python interpreter lifecycle blender python interpreter lifecycle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","fileName":"Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Embedded Python Internals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender BPY API","Blender Built-in Python Module Registration","Blender Python Global Interpreter Lock","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python interpreter lifecycle blender python interpreter lifecycle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","fileName":"Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle","heading":"Blender Python Interpreter Lifecycle","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender prepares its built-in extension table before calling CPython's initialization function. Once the interpreter is active, the application manually exposes Blender modules as needed, executes scripts during operation, and calls the matching finalization path during shutdown.\n\nThe [[Blender BPY API]] packages this sequence as start, end, and reset operations invoked from the window manager. Correct ordering matters because [[Blender Built-in Python Module Registration]] mu